GB: Maginot.

INT: Sorry.

GB: Well, the Germans had their so-called impregnable fortress called a Siegfried Line, which stretched all along the German borders from-- separated Germany-- I mean, the border from Luxembourg, Belgium, and France. They called it the Siegfried Line, while the French had their fortress line called Maginot Line.

